% The gchord codes g, h, i, j, k play the notes of a guitar chord, and G,
% H, I, J, K the same notes an octave lower.  A code past the last note of
% a shorter chord plays that last note, so that an Alberti bass has no
% gap: j on "C" plays G, and h, i, j on "C5" play G.  dogchords()
% (genmidi.c) used to play the slot after the last note instead, left
% from an earlier chord or 0, a missing break made k also play G, and K
% read the fifth note of a four-note chord.  A chord in lower case, as
% "c", has the bass note only: f plays it and g, h, i play nothing.
X:1
T:Gchord codes g to k and G to K
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/2
Q:1/4=120
K:C
%%MIDI gchord ghij
"C"CE|"C5"CG|"G7"B,D|
%%MIDI gchord hijk
"C9"CE|"G7"B,D|"C"CE|
%%MIDI gchord GHIJ
"C"CE|"C5"CG|
%%MIDI gchord HIJK
"C9"CE|"G7"B,D|
%%MIDI gchord fghi
"c"CE|]
